(271, 'anggā', 'a nggā : 1. will, to want to; tan a nggā will not, not to want to; m will, to want to, to be inclined to. 2. (S) body; trunk; makāngga to have the body of; pinakāngga to be made center; to be the center (of). Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 9),
