(279, 'adak', 'a dak : in- a dak trampled down, crushed under the foot; pushed a side. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 3),
(280, 'anapatya', 'a napatya : (S) childless; a napatyā to hope to be childlessl; willbe chilsless. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 5),
