(284, 'ampět', 'a mpět : māmpět stopped; in endured; closed, shut; tan a mpět unbearable, insupportable. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 5),
(285, 'ampěh', 'a mpěh : a ng to stop; to stand, to bear, to endure; māmpěh to stop, to decrease; tan a mpěh continuously, incessantly. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 5),
