(850, 'baris', 'b aris (barIs) : lêbar, mrucut, b aris. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 8),
(851, 'barla', 'b arla (barlO) : warni, jêmparing b arla. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 4),
(852, 'bok rantèn', 'b ok rantèn (bOk rantEn) : b ok ngantèn. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 5),
(853, 'budi', 'b udi () : b udi, manah. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 7),
(854, 'bêsmi', 'b êsmi (b|smi) : gêsang, b êsmi, ka. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 9),
(855, 'bawat', 'b awat () : songsong b awat. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 4),
(856, 'bala', 'b ala (bOlO) : pagêr, b ala. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 6),
(857, 'bela', 'b ela (belO) : tumut, b ela, amni, tampi. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 6),
(858, 'balik', 'b alik (balI?) : tulak, wangsul, sungsang, b alik. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 1),
(859, 'bolang', 'b olang (bolaG) : catur, amêngan b olang, kasukan catur. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 9),
(860, 'baya', 'b aya (bOyO) : pakèwêd, jangjang, b ilahi, gawat, b êning, b aya. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 8),
(861, 'bimana', 'b imana (bimOnO) : murka, linangkung ing manah, agêng; wara b imana: tiyang agêng. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 6),
(862, 'babahan', 'b abahan () : b abahan. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 6),
(863, 'bubuk', 'b ubuk (bubU?) : upas b ubuk. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 6),
(864, 'babud', 'b abud (babUd) : b abud. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 10),
(865, 'bêbêd', 'b êbêd (b|b|d) : b êbêd. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 9),
(866, 'batharaberawa', 'b athara b erawa (baTOrO berOwO) : jêjulukipun B athara Kala. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 3),
(867, 'bangsa', 'b angsa (baGsO) : b ăngsa. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 4),
(868, 'bangga', 'b angga (baGgO) : wangkot, mogok, sarosa, ukara, rosa, b ăngga, nglawan, sikara. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 7),
(869, 'bungbang', 'b ungbang (buGbaG) : nglowong, wungwang, pring b ungbang, pring wungwang. Têmbung Kawi Mawi Têgêsipun, Wintêr, 1928, #1506.', 1),
(870, 'bangun', 'b angun (baGUn) : I 1 tangi; 2 (ut. gagat- b angun), ayah esuk. II di-[x]: 1 digawe; 2 ([x] anyar): dianyarake. Kawi - Jarwa, Poerwadarminta, 1943, #1856.', 8),
(871, 'mardawa-basa', 'mardawa- b asa (mardOwO­bOsO) : ahli b asa. Kawi - Jarwa, Poerwadarminta, 1943, #1856.', 1),
(872, 'ulu-bêkti', 'ulu- b êkti (ulu­b|kti) : (-pêkti): b ulu- b êkti. Kawi - Jarwa, Poerwadarminta, 1943, #1856.', 10),
(873, 'babar', 'b abar : 1 to proliferate. Sajrone sak jam wae kewan siji b isa [x] dadi satus. Inside of an hour, a single germ can develop into 100. [x]-e wiji manungsa the procreation of the human race. 2 to unfold, open out. [x]-ing lakon the unfolding of the plot. [x]-e priyayi sing nyalawadi disclosure of the guilty ... selengkapnya b abar : 1 to proliferate. Sajrone sak jam wae kewan siji b isa [x] dadi satus. Inside of an hour, a single germ can develop into 100. [x]-e wiji manungsa the procreation of the human race. 2 to unfold, open out. [x]-ing lakon the unfolding of the plot. [x]-e priyayi sing nyalawadi disclosure of the guilty person. 3 to b e b orn (ki for LAIR). [x]-an 1 product, output. B êbêde [x]-an Sala. His b atik skirt is from Solo. 2 revelation of the truth at the end of a story. 3 b irth (ki for KÊ-LAIR-AN); to give b irth (ki for NG-LAIR-AKE). 4 ritual meal celebrating a b irth. 5 dyeing of b atik. [x]-ane mancêp. The dye took. m/di-[x] 1 to spread sth. m-[x] êlar to spread the wings. m-[x] ganda wangi to exude a sweet fragrance. 2 to produce, put out. m-[x] prahoto to manufacture trucks. kalawarta kang di-[x] ing Jakarta a newspaper published in Jakarta. 3 to give b irth (ki for NG-LAIR-AKE). m-[x] putra lanang to b ear a son. 4 to dye [ b atik]. 5 to remove the wax from fabric after each dyeing in the b atik-making process. m/di-[x]-ake 1 to spread sth. m-[x]-ake layar to spread sails. 2 to proliferate sth. Manungsa wajib m-[x]-ake tuwuh. It is man''sduty to procreate himself. 3 to disclose, unfold. m-[x]-ake wadi to let out a secret. pa-m-[x] spreading; procreation. See also B ABAR-PISAN. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(874, 'bayonèt', 'b ayonèt : b ayonet. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(875, 'banggèl', 'b anggèl : m-[x] var of M- B ANGGÈL. m/di-[x] 1 to snap at (as though to b ite). 2 to give a rebuttal (in debating). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(876, 'bebas', 'b ebas : var of B EBAS. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(877, 'bèbrèl', 'b èbrèl : var of B ÊBRÊL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(878, 'bangêt', 'b angêt : ng, sangêt kr 1 very (much), considerable, altogether. dhuwur [x] very tall. klèru [x] very much mistaken. [x] ngarêp-arêp to look forward to eagerly. [x] ditrêsnani. She loves him very much. [x] b ungahe. He was delighted. nyêngkane [x] at the very most. Kula rujuk sangêt. I quite agree. Aku ora ... selengkapnya b angêt : ng, sangêt kr 1 very (much), considerable, altogether. dhuwur [x] very tall. klèru [x] very much mistaken. [x] ngarêp-arêp to look forward to eagerly. [x] ditrêsnani. She loves him very much. [x] b ungahe. He was delighted. nyêngkane [x] at the very most. Kula rujuk sangêt. I quite agree. Aku ora nyana [x] yèn arêp dadi kêtua. I had no idea I was to b e chairman. 2 serious, intense. lêlara [x] a severe illness. Ing mangsa kêtiga panase [x]. The heat is terrible in the dry season. [x] ênggone gawe rusak. It did severe damage. Sangsaya sangêt gumunipun. He b ecame more and more astonished. Aja [x]-[x]. Don''t overdo it. 3 emphatic. Tak jaluk kanthi [x] kowe aja mèlu edan-edanan. I b eg you not to get involved in that mess. kê-[x]-ên excessive. Rada kê-[x]-ên olèhmu sujanan. You''re b eing overcautious. Kê-[x]-ên b angêt olèhmu ngrugèkake nêgara. The damage caused to the nation was incalculable. m/di-[x]-ake 1 to make sth worse. 2 ro emphasize, exaggerate. pa-m-[x] emphasis. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(879, 'bêlang', 'b êlang : 1 skin b lemish. 2 white spot(s) on an animal''s coat. Si B êlang Spotty (the dog). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(880, 'bêluk', 'b êluk : 1 a certain caterpillar. 1 a variety of owl. 3 smoke, steam. m/di-[x] 1 to turn. m-[x] nêngên to turn (to the) right. 2 to call to, yell at. 3 to b end; to b end out of shape. [x] a-n-tanjak to follow one''s own inclinations. See also KUKUK- B ÊLUK. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(881, 'bêndhêl', 'b êndhêl : var of B ÈNDHÊL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(882, 'bêndho', 'b êndho : large- b laded knife for cutting wood. m/di-[x] to cut [wood] with a b êndho. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(883, 'bengkong', 'b engkong : b èngkong, curved, crooked, b ent. Pite rodhane ngarêp [x]. The front wheel of his b icycle is crooked. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(884, 'bètèr', 'b ètèr : b ètêr, 1 b itters. 2 var of B LÈTÊR. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(885, 'blêgèr', 'b lêgèr : var of B LÊGÊR. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(886, 'blelu', 'b lelu : b lèlu, rg var of B LILU. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(887, 'blimbing', 'b limbing : a tart yellow fruit about the size of a mango. [x]-an resembling this fruit. [x] lingir a dessert variety of this fruit. [x] wuluh a small sour b limbing used in cooking. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(888, 'bramani', 'b ramani : var of B RAMANI. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(889, 'braok', 'b raok : (or b roak-[x] or m-[x]) loud, shrill. Swarane b raok-[x]. She has a piercing voice. [x]-an a shrill-voiced person. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(890, 'brengos', 'b rengos : var of B RÊNGOS. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(891, 'Budha', 'B udha : var sp of B UDHA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(892, 'bujung', 'b ujung : sugar-cane leaf (kr for GODHONG TÊBU). m/di-[x] to chase, go after. A mlajar dipun b ujung B . B ran after A. M-[x] dhuwit Rp 100 malah kelangan Rp 2000. He tried for 100 rupiahs and lost 2000. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(893, 'bu(w)-', 'b u(w)- : see also under B U-, B W- (Introduction, 2.9.7). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(894, 'akarbahar', 'akar b ahar [Ind] : akar b ahar. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 4),
(895, 'arangbatu', 'arang b atu [Ind] : arêng b atu. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 7),
(896, 'bab', 'b ab [Ind] : 1 gapura; 2 b ab. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 8),
