(2396, 'citta', 'c itta : (S) ideal; thought; feeling; inner self, internal, heart, back of one;s mind; c initta thought, felt. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 5),
(2397, 'cittajña', 'c ittajña : (S) c lear-sighted; thought reading, mind reading. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 6),
(2398, 'citra', 'c itra : (S) c lear, bright; splendid, fine; various; letter; painting; picture; manitra multicolored; c initra decorated. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 7),
(2399, 'citramegha', 'c itramegha : (S) gleaming c loud. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 5),
(2400, 'citralikita', 'c itralikita : (S c itralikhita) painted; described. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 4),
(2401, 'cidra', 'c idra : (S c hidra) trick, ruse, lie, deceit; hole; want, shortage; unguarded place; añidra- c inidra to deceive one another; c umidra to deceive; ka deceived; taken in the act; visible; silih c idra to deceive each other. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 9),
(2402, 'cintāmoha', 'c intāmoha : (S) c onfused, at wit''s end. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 6),
(2403, 'cilu', 'c ilu : kapa to float away (with the c urrent); to be c arried away (by the flood). Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 3),
(2404, 'cīwara', 'c īwara : (S) beggar''s c lothing; a to wear a beggar''s c oat. Kawi Lexicon, Wojowasito, 1980, #575.', 6),
