(3781, 'èjèg', 'è jèg : 1 to jog, run with small steps. 2 to keep saying/asking sth. ng-[x] 1 to jog. 2 to keep dropping in. [x] è lèr to say/ask again and again. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3782, 'edong', 'e dong : [x]-[x] or e dang-[x] to have difficulty walking, e .g. after being circumcised. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
