(3784, 'ègèng', 'è gèng : e gang-[x] to have difficulty walking. ng-[x] to walk with difficulty. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3785, 'egle', 'e gle : è glèg, è glèh, è glèng var of E GLA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3786, 'ègrèk', 'è grèk : flimsy (var of È KRÈK). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3787, 'èyèg', 'è yèg : restless. e yag-[x] to keep fidgeting restlessly. ng-[x] to move about restlessly. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3788, 'èyèl', 'è yèl : [x]-[x]-an to argue with e ach sticking to his own view. ng-[x] stubborn, unwilling to yield. ng/di-[x]-(i) to argue with [smn] from sheer obstinacy. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3789, 'eka', 'e ka : 1 oj one. 2 unity, agreement. [x]-n 1 unity, agreement. 2 the unit digit in a number. Taun 1957 e kane pitu. The digit in the unit place of year-number 1957 is 7. [x]-n, dasan, atusan, e won units, tens, hundreds, thousands. têmbung [x]-n number, counting word. ng/di-[x]-[x] to think [about], reflect. ... selengkapnya e ka : 1 oj one. 2 unity, agreement. [x]-n 1 unity, agreement. 2 the unit digit in a number. Taun 1957 e kane pitu. The digit in the unit place of year-number 1957 is 7. [x]-n, dasan, atusan, e won units, tens, hundreds, thousands. têmbung [x]-n number, counting word. ng/di-[x]-[x] to think [about], reflect. sa-[x] in agreement; sa-[x]-praja in cooperation for a common goal. Wong-wong sa-[x]-praja arêp ndandani sêkolah kuwi. The people are pooling their e fforts to repair the school. saiyêg [x]-praja a joint e ffort. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3790, 'ekapraja', 'e kapraja : see E KA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3791, 'èkèh', 'è kèh : see E KAH. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3792, 'ekrok', 'e krok : e krak-[x] unsteady loose in the joints. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3793, 'êksêtra(h)', 'ê ksêtra(h) : e t cetera. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3794, 'èksi', 'è ksi : e ye (oj). k(a)-[x] visible, in sight. mang-[x] ltry to watch, observe. ng/di-[x] ltry to look at, see. (ng)-[x]-ganda ltry name of the historic Mataram kingdom. pa-ng-[x] vision, sight. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3795, 'èksportir', 'è ksportir : e xporter. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3796, 'èkstra(h)', 'è kstra(h) : e xtra. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3797, 'èkstrak', 'è kstrak : flavoring e xtract. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3798, 'êlak', 'ê lak : place where a small water channel e mpties. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3799, 'êlastis', 'ê lastis : flexible, e lastic. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3800, 'elèktris', 'e lèktris : e lectric; e lectricity. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3801, 'elèktro', 'e lèktro : var of E LÈKTRIS. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3802, 'elèktronik', 'e lèktronik : e lèktronis, e lectronic(s). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3803, 'êlho', 'ê lho : e xcl (var sp of LO). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3804, 'èlmi', 'è lmi : sbst? kr for È LMU. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3805, 'êlo', 'ê lo : e xcl (var sp of LO). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3806, 'êm', 'ê m : e xcl e xpressing hesitation. [x], wêdi aku. I''m [too] scared [to go]. [x], aku dhewe durung ngêrti jalarane mati. Well ... I don''t know myself what caused her death. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3807, 'email', 'e mail : 1 tooth e namel. 2 porcelain glaze. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3808, 'êmak', 'ê mak : 1 maidservant who takes care of the children. 2 mother, mom (var of Ê MBOK). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3809, 'eman', 'e man : unfortunate, regrettable; to regret. [x]- e unfortunately. [x]- e dhèke ora bisa cara Inggris. It''s too bad he can''t speak E nglish. [x]-[x] regrettable. Ah [x]-[x] têmên, bêbêd suwèk. Oh, what a pity - the skirt is torn. ng/di-[x] to care about, have concern for. [x] karo to care for deeply. Dhèke [x] ... selengkapnya e man : unfortunate, regrettable; to regret. [x]- e unfortunately. [x]- e dhèke ora bisa cara Inggris. It''s too bad he can''t speak E nglish. [x]-[x] regrettable. Ah [x]-[x] têmên, bêbêd suwèk. Oh, what a pity - the skirt is torn. ng/di-[x] to care about, have concern for. [x] karo to care for deeply. Dhèke [x] karo bojone. He cherishes his wife. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3810, 'emansipasi', 'e mansipasi : e mancipation. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3811, 'èlu', 'è lu : to accompany (childish var of M-[x] below). e la-[x] to do what others are doing, go along with the crowd. [x]-n(-[x]-n) ê n 1 to tag along with people habitually. 2 to side with smn in an argument. k-[x] to be carried along (with). A tansah dipêpengin si B, banjur k-[x]. B kept coaxing A and A finally ... selengkapnya è lu : to accompany (childish var of M-[x] below). e la-[x] to do what others are doing, go along with the crowd. [x]-n(-[x]-n) ê n 1 to tag along with people habitually. 2 to side with smn in an argument. k-[x] to be carried along (with). A tansah dipêpengin si B, banjur k-[x]. B kept coaxing A and A finally gave in. Saka baude caturan nganti wong-wong akèh sing padha k-[x] katut. He''s such a smooth talker that many people fall for it. m-[x] (tumut kr, n-dhèrèk ka) 1 to accompany, join in, [do] with. Dhèke m-[x] mênyang pasar. He went with her to the marketplace. Aku m-[x] kuliah. I attended the lectures. m-[x] lotre to participate in a lottery. Slamêt ora m-[x] mlêbu. Slamet didn''t go in with the others. 2 to live with and be supported by. Wong tuwane m-[x] anake. The parents live with their son. m-[x] grubyug to jump on the bandwagon. m-[x]-m-[x] to butt in; to tag along. Siti m-mèlu clathu: Iya aku m-[x]. Siti chimed in: I want to go too. ng-[x] to go along with the crowd. ng/di-[x]-kake (n/dipun-tumut-akên kr, n/di-dhèrèk-ake ka) 1 to have smn go along with [a person]. 2 to have smn live with and be supported by [smn, usu. a relative]. Anake dielokake bulike. She sent her son to live with his aunt. ng/di-[x]-ni to go along with smn as a companion or servant. A ora gêlêm dièloni B. A didn''t want B to go with him as retainer. See also ILU. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3812, 'êmbag', 'ê mbag : var of Ê MBÊG. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3813, 'embal', 'e mbal : var of E PAH. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3814, 'êmban', 'ê mban : nursemaid (usu. a woman). ê mbok [x] female nursemaid. [x]-[x]
(p-atur a -an ki) batik shawl for carrying a child slung
from the shoulder. [x]-an the part of a ring where the stone is
set. [x]-[x]-an child being carried in a shawl. ng/di-[x] to carry
a child in a shawl on one''s chest. ng-[x] ... selengkapnya ê mban : nursemaid (usu. a woman). ê mbok [x] female nursemaid. [x]-[x] (p-atur a -an ki) batik shawl for carrying a child slung from the shoulder. [x]-an the part of a ring where the stone is set. [x]-[x]-an child being carried in a shawl. ng/di-[x] to carry a child in a shawl on one''s chest. ng-[x] dhawuh to carry out an order. ng/di-[x]-ake to carry a child for smn. ng/di-[x]-i to serve as a nursemaid to/for. [x] cindhe a child-carrying shawl of fine soft material; [x] cindhe [x] silad-an to play favorites; biased, partial. Dadi guru ora kêna [x] cindhe [x] siladan karo murid-muride kabèh. A teacher mustn''t treat any pupils differently from others. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3815, 'èmbèl', 'è mbèl : [x]-[x] supplement, postscript. ng/di-[x]-[x]-i to add a little something to. Karanganmu iki wis apik, ora pêrlu di-[x]-[x]-i manèh. Your article is just fine now; don''t put anything e lse in. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3816, 'êmblog', 'ê mblog : roll, bolt (of fabric). [x]-[x]-an 1 in large quantities; e xtensive. 2 in rolls; by the roll. mori [x]-[x]-an a bolt of cambric. ng/di-[x] to apply thickly. Gambare di-[x] cèt abang. He plastered red paint on the picture. See also BLOG. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3817, 'êmbong', 'ê mbong : var of Ê MBOK. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3818, 'èmbrèh', 'è mbrèh : 1 sweeping the ground [of e xcessively long clothing]. 2 having a clean or neat appearance. 3 not poor and not rich; having e nough for one''s needs. ng-[x] sweeping the ground [of long clothing]. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3819, 'èmbrèt', 'è mbrèt : ê mbrèt, worker who is paid by the day. ng-[x] to travel at low cost in a carriage hired by a group. ng/di-[x]-ake to hire work done by the day. Aku ng-[x]-ake kumbahan. I have smn do my laundry e ach day. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3820, 'êmbut', 'ê mbut : ( ê mbat kr?) [x]-[x]-an [of fruits] softened by pounding to release the juices inside. m-[x] soft, mushy. ng/di-[x]-[x] to soften [fruit] as above. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3821, 'emigrasi', 'e migrasi : e migration. ng/di-[x]-kake to cause to e migrate. Akèh pêndhudhuk diemigrasèkake ing pulo mau. Many of the people were sent to that island to live. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(3822, 'emyah', 'e myah : var of È MYÈH. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3823, 'emod', 'e mod : var of È MU. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3824, 'emor', 'e mor : var or È MU. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3825, 'êmprèt', 'ê mprèt : ng-[x] [of e lephants] to trumpet. ng/di-[x]-(i) to scoff at, look down on. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3826, 'êmprit', 'ê mprit : a certain small hummingbird (considered an omen of danger). [x] a-buntut bêdhug to make a mountain out of a molehill. [x] gantil 1 a variety of the above bird (the seeing of which is considered a death wish). 2 roof e mbellishment. [x] kaji a white-headed variety of the above bird. [x] tondhang a ... selengkapnya ê mprit : a certain small hummingbird (considered an omen of danger). [x] a-buntut bêdhug to make a mountain out of a molehill. [x] gantil 1 a variety of the above bird (the seeing of which is considered a death wish). 2 roof e mbellishment. [x] kaji a white-headed variety of the above bird. [x] tondhang a variety of the above bird. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3827, 'êmpur', 'ê mpur : [x]-[x] or ( e sp). m-[x] pleasantly mealy in the center [of cooked cassava, sweet potato]. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3828, '-ên', 'ê n : (-nên after vowel) 1 (ng) psv imperative suffix. Dêlêng- ê n. Look (at it)! Pring kae gawa-nên mrene. Bring that bamboo over here. 2 suffix for a bodily process or condition. Drijine gêtih- ê n. His finger bled. Matane walang- ê n. His e yes bugged out. aras-aras- ê n nyambut gawe lackadaisical toward one''s ... selengkapnya - ê n : (-nên after vowel) 1 (ng) psv imperative suffix. Dêlêng- ê n. Look (at it)! Pring kae gawa-nên mrene. Bring that bamboo over here. 2 suffix for a bodily process or condition. Drijine gêtih- ê n. His finger bled. Matane walang- ê n. His e yes bugged out. aras-aras- ê n nyambut gawe lackadaisical toward one''s work. mata dhuwit- ê n money-mad. 3 second e lement of KA ... Ê N circumfix. k-adhêm- ê n too cold. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3829, 'endha', 'e ndha : to e lude, dodge. [x] mangiwa [x] mênêngên kaya prênjak tinaji (wy) clever and agile at e luding one''s e nemies. (m)-[x]-(m)-[x] to disguise oneself. Dhèke m-mendha dadi bakul bêras. He posed as a rice seller. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3830, 'êndhak', 'ê ndhak : [x]-[x] cacing medicine for stomach worms. m-[x] 1 to subside. Nêsune wis m-[x]. His anger has cooled. Liwête wis m-[x]. The rice has almost stopped boiling. 2 to stoop, duck. 3 to walk in a squatting position in the presence of an e xalted person, to show humility. m-[x] m-pêndhukul full of ups and ... selengkapnya ê ndhak : [x]-[x] cacing medicine for stomach worms. m-[x] 1 to subside. Nêsune wis m-[x]. His anger has cooled. Liwête wis m-[x]. The rice has almost stopped boiling. 2 to stoop, duck. 3 to walk in a squatting position in the presence of an e xalted person, to show humility. m-[x] m-pêndhukul full of ups and downs. Dalane m-[x]-mêndhukul. The road is hilly (bumpy). ng/di-[x]-ake to cause to subside. A bisa ng-[x]-ake nêsune B. A managed to calm B down. ng/di-[x]-i to bow to smn. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3831, 'èndêl', 'è ndêl : act of stopping (kr for ANDHÊG). k-[x] to (come to a) stop (kr for M-ANDHÊG, M- Ê NDHÊG). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3832, 'èndhèl', 'è ndhèl : 1 half-gron Manila duckling (young of the E NTHOG). 2 female servant. 3 child. [x]-[x] e mbellishment, accompaniment, suplement. ng-[x] to accompany; to supplement. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3833, 'êndhêl', 'ê ndhêl : one who can be relied upon; one who is e ntrusted with sth. ng/di-[x] to believe (in), trust. ng/di-[x]-ake to put too much faith in, rely on too heavily. Aja sok ng-[x]-ake kêkuatanmu. Don''t overestimate your strength. See also ANDHÊL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3834, 'êndêm', 'ê ndêm : stupor caused by liquor or drugs. [x]-[x]-an to get intoxicated deliberately; a party held for this purpose. Bubar ujian bocah-bocah têrus padha [x]-[x]-an. After the e xam, the boys had a drinking party. k-[x]-an (kê-wurun ki) under the e ffect of drink/drugs. m-[x] (wuru ki) 1 intoxicated; drugged. ... selengkapnya ê ndêm : stupor caused by liquor or drugs. [x]-[x]-an to get intoxicated deliberately; a party held for this purpose. Bubar ujian bocah-bocah têrus padha [x]-[x]-an. After the e xam, the boys had a drinking party. k-[x]-an (kê-wurun ki) under the e ffect of drink/drugs. m-[x] (wuru ki) 1 intoxicated; drugged. 2 slang crazy about smn, sth. [x] gênje e ccentric, queer. m-[x] sêgara seasick(ness). m-[x]-i intoxicating. ng-[x]-i 1 intoxicating; having a stupefying e ffect. 2 (psv di-[x]-i) to get smn drunk/drugged. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3835, 'èndhèr', 'è ndhèr : ng/di-[x]-ake 1 to e xplain (inf var of NG/DI-ANDHAR-AKE). 2 to reveal, disclose. Aja sênêng ng-[x]-[x]-ake wadining wong tuwa. Don''t tell family secrets! Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3836, 'êndhih', 'ê ndhih : k-[x] to lose, get overpowered. ng/di-[x] 1 to beat, overcome. 2 to take over, preempt. ng-[x] panggonan to take smn e lse''s seat. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3837, 'ênjah', 'ê njah : ng/di-[x]-[x] slang to want to have e verything available. Pilihên salah siji, aja sênêng ng-[x]-[x]. Pick one - don''t try to get them all. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3838, 'ènjèr', 'è njèr : (or [x]-an) wy (to e ngage in) preliminaries to a fighting scene (depicted in a dance), during which the opponents size up e ach other''s fighting strength. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3839, 'enjing', 'e njing : morning (kr for E SUK). See also BENJING. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3840, 'èngès', 'è ngès : ng/di-[x] 1 to sharpen (the e nd of). 2 to show [the teeth]. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3841, 'enggal', 'e nggal : 1 quickly, right away (kr for Ê NDANG?). [x] mrenea. Come here, quick! 2 new; recent (kr for ANYAR). [x]-ing carita to make a long story short ... [x]-[x] as quickly as possible (kr for AGE-AGE?). [x]-[x]-an in a great hurry. Kok [x]-[x]-an, diunjuk dhisik kopine. What''s the hurry? - drink your cofee ... selengkapnya e nggal : 1 quickly, right away (kr for Ê NDANG?). [x] mrenea. Come here, quick! 2 new; recent (kr for ANYAR). [x]-ing carita to make a long story short ... [x]-[x] as quickly as possible (kr for AGE-AGE?). [x]-[x]-an in a great hurry. Kok [x]-[x]-an, diunjuk dhisik kopine. What''s the hurry? - drink your cofee first! ng/di-[x]-ake to speed sth up. [x] iki ([x] mangke kr) just recently. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3842, 'ênggêl', 'ê nggêl : main ( e ssential, central) part. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3843, 'ênggo', 'ê nggo : (usu. prn nggo) ng, ê ngge kr used as (shf of KANGGO). Kêrtas kuwi nggo apa? What''s that paper to? di-[x] inf var of DI-ANGGO. Papan kuwi dinggo rapat mêngko sore. That place is to be used for a meeting this afternoon. See also ANGGO, KANGGO. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3844, 'ênggok', 'ê nggok : 1 in, at, on. Omahe nggok ê ndi? Where does he live? 2 throat (inf var of GOROK-AN). [x]-[x] 1 inf throat. 2 ointment for the throat and neck. ng/di-[x]-i to place sth smw. Mejane dinggoki kêmbang. She put flowers on the table. Anake dinggoki klambi abang. She dressed her daughter in red. ... selengkapnya ê nggok : 1 in, at, on. Omahe nggok ê ndi? Where does he live? 2 throat (inf var of GOROK-AN). [x]-[x] 1 inf throat. 2 ointment for the throat and neck. ng/di-[x]-i to place sth smw. Mejane dinggoki kêmbang. She put flowers on the table. Anake dinggoki klambi abang. She dressed her daughter in red. ng/di-[x]-[x]-i to apply medication to the throat and neck. See also MANGGOK. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3845, 'ênggos', 'ê nggos : ê ngga-[x] out of breath. See also KRÊNGGOS. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3846, 'ênggrik', 'ê nggrik : var of Ê NGGÈK. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3847, 'engkol', 'e ngkol : 1 wrench; curved wrench handle. 2 strange; roundabout. 3 unit of measurement: the distance from e lbow to fingertips. sa-[x] one such unit. [x]-[x] or e ngkal-[x] zigzag. Dalane e ngkal-[x]. The road twists and turns. Taplake meja dokokana [x]-[x]. Put decorative zigzags on the tablecloth. ng-[x] 1 ... selengkapnya e ngkol : 1 wrench; curved wrench handle. 2 strange; roundabout. 3 unit of measurement: the distance from e lbow to fingertips. sa-[x] one such unit. [x]-[x] or e ngkal-[x] zigzag. Dalane e ngkal-[x]. The road twists and turns. Taplake meja dokokana [x]-[x]. Put decorative zigzags on the tablecloth. ng-[x] 1 twisting and turning. Dalane kok ng-[x]. How the road winds! 2 (psv di-[x]) to measure sth in units as above (3). ng/di-[x]-ake to turn or bend sth. See also MENGKOL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3848, 'engkrah', 'e ngkrah : sa-[x]-[x]- e whatever smn does. Sa-[x]-[x]- e didêlêng wae. Observe e verything he does. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3849, 'engkrang', 'e ngkrang : a certain style of Jogjanese male classical dancing. sa-[x]-[x]- e whatever smn does. Sa-[x]-[x]- e njèngkèlke. E verything he does is irritating. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3850, 'ènsiklopedhi', 'è nsiklopedhi : e ncyclopedia. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3851, 'ênthe', 'ê nthe : intsfr e arly [in the late-afternoon period]. sore [x]-[x] first thing in the e vening. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3852, 'èntèh', 'è ntèh : var of Ê NTHE. Isih sore [x] wis turu. It''s e arly in the e vening but he''s already gone to bed! Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3853, 'èntên', 'è ntên : to e xist; there is/are (md for ANA a ). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3854, 'ènthèng', 'è nthèng : light (i. e . not heavy; not difficult; not serious). Kupu iku [x] bangêt awake. Butterflies have light bodies. Pêgaweane [x]. The work is light. Larane wis [x]. His illness has improved. [x]-an to e njoy helping others. [x]-an bau to e njoy helping others with manual labor. k-[x]- ê n e xcessively light. ... selengkapnya è nthèng : light (i. e . not heavy; not difficult; not serious). Kupu iku [x] bangêt awake. Butterflies have light bodies. Pêgaweane [x]. The work is light. Larane wis [x]. His illness has improved. [x]-an to e njoy helping others. [x]-an bau to e njoy helping others with manual labor. k-[x]- ê n e xcessively light. ng/di-[x]-ake 1 to make sth light. 2 to make light of, not take seriously. ng-[x]-i to recover. Ali wis ng-[x]-i. Ali is getting better. [x] lambe to talk a lot; to e ngage in gossip. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(3855, 'êntèng', 'ê ntèng : [x]-[x] intsfr all gone (var of Ê NTING). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3856, 'êncêb', 'ê ncêb : ng/di-[x]-i 1 to stick sth into [soil e tc.]. 2 to cling fast to. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(3857, 'èncêp', 'è ncêp : m-[x] to twist the lips quickly to one side as a gesture of dislike, contempt. m- e ncap-m-[x] to make the above gesture repeatedly. ng/di-[x]-ake to twist [the lips] in this gesture. Lambene di-[x]-ake. She gestured disdainfully. ng/di-[x]-i to gesture at [smn] as above. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3858, 'ênci:m', 'ê nci:m : sister. ng/di-[x] to long for, have one''s e ye on. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3859, 'ênclok', 'ê nclok : var of E NCOK. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3860, 'enco', 'e nco : comfortable, e asy, pleasant. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3861, 'encos', 'e ncos : m-[x] slantwise, crooked, lopsided. m- e ncas-m-[x] pl as above. Tulisane mencas-m-[x]. His handwriting goes e very which way. ng-[x] slantwise, on the diagonal. Playune ng-[x] ngiwa. He ran off to the left. Wite dikêthok ng-[x]. He cut the tree off slantwise. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3862, 'entos', 'e ntos : e nthos, able; capable. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3863, 'êntos', 'ê ntos : to wait (root form: kr for Ê NTI). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3864, 'êntrog', 'ê ntrog : ng/di-[x]-[x] or ng/di- ê ntrag-[x] to shake (up). Aku tau di-[x]-[x] bis. I got jounced around on the bus. ng/di-[x]-(ake) to shake sth; to trample on sth. See also ANTROG. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3865, 'entuk', 'e ntuk : ng, (pik)antuk kr 1 to get, obtain. Kuwi gèk [x]-mu saka ngêndi? Where did you get that? Aku wis [x] pêgaweyan liya. I''ve found another job. [x] pènsiun to receive a pension. 2 to receive permission. Kowe ora [x] lunga. You aren''t allowed to go. 3 to receive as spouse. Ê ntèk- ê ntèkane Slamêt [x] ... selengkapnya e ntuk : ng, (pik)antuk kr 1 to get, obtain. Kuwi gèk [x]-mu saka ngêndi? Where did you get that? Aku wis [x] pêgaweyan liya. I''ve found another job. [x] pènsiun to receive a pension. 2 to receive permission. Kowe ora [x] lunga. You aren''t allowed to go. 3 to receive as spouse. Ê ntèk- ê ntèkane Slamêt [x] Siti. Slamet finally married Siti. [x](-[x])an ng only thing(s) obtained, e .g. a harvest; the answer to a problem; profits from sales; stolen loot. ng/di-[x]-ake ng only to allow, let. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(3866, 'era', 'e ra : [of e yes] not functioning together, out of focus with e ach other. mata [x] wall- e yed; cross- e yed. See also KERA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3867, 'èrèb', 'è rèb : ng/di-[x](-[x]) to drag smn along; to involve smn e lse in [a nefarious activity]. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3868, 'èrêp', 'è rêp : e state, property. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3869, 'Eropa(h)', 'E ropa(h) : E urope. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3870, 'èru', 'è ru : e ra-[x] tumult, violent disorder. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3871, 'ês', 'ê s : 1 shoo! scat! 2 sound of disapproval. Ê ssss, omong kosong iku. It''s a lie! 3 pst! di-[x] to be addressed in one of the above ways. Dhèke tansah di-[x] ing Sujana. Sujono kept saying "pst!" to her. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3872, 'èsprès', 'è sprès : 1 fast. Yèn [x] bayar dhobêl. If you want it fast, you have to pay double. 2 e xpress train. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(3873, 'èstu', 'è stu : sms SA-[x] below. [x]-nipun sms SA-[x]-NIPUN. ng-[x] pada to do homage to, show e steem for. ng/di-[x]-kake 1 to obey. È stokna dhawuhing guru. Do as the teacher says. 2 to laugh (oblique ka for NG(GÊ)-GUYU). ng/dipun-[x]-kakên to carry out an intention (kr for NY/DI-SIDA-KAKE). sa-[x] 1 really, ... selengkapnya è stu : sms SA-[x] below. [x]-nipun sms SA-[x]-NIPUN. ng-[x] pada to do homage to, show e steem for. ng/di-[x]-kake 1 to obey. È stokna dhawuhing guru. Do as the teacher says. 2 to laugh (oblique ka for NG(GÊ)-GUYU). ng/dipun-[x]-kakên to carry out an intention (kr for NY/DI-SIDA-KAKE). sa-[x] 1 really, actually (kr for NYATA, TÊMÊN(AN). 2 to go through with, succeed in [do]ing (kr for SIDA). sa-[x]-nipun actually, in fact (kr for NYATA-NE, SA-TÊMÊN- E ). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3874, 'êt', 'ê t : e xcl e xpressing surpise, dismay, warning. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3875, 'êt-', 'ê t- : ê th-, see also under T-, TH- (Introduction, 2.9.5). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3876, 'ètêr', 'è têr : var sp of È THÊR. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(3877, 'êtêr', 'ê têr : ng-[x]-[x]-i e art-shaking; causing smn to tremble. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3878, 'èthêr', 'è thêr : (prn è têr) e ther. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(3879, 'etikèt', 'e tikèt : manners, e tiquette. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(3880, 'ethos', 'e thos : var of E THOR. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3881, 'evolusi', 'e volusi : e volution. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3882, 'ewa', 'e wa : of an unsympathetic or jealous nature. ng/di-[x]-k-[x]-kake to act supercilious (toward), treat with disdain. mèsêm ngk-ngewakake to smile in a superior way. [x] dene or [x] mêngkono or [x] sêmono e ven so; but still; in spite of [the foregoing]. Wis diajar barang, [x] sêmono ora kapok. He''s been ... selengkapnya e wa : of an unsympathetic or jealous nature. ng/di-[x]-k-[x]-kake to act supercilious (toward), treat with disdain. mèsêm ngewak-ngewakake to smile in a superior way. [x] dene or [x] mêngkono or [x] sêmono e ven so; but still; in spite of [the foregoing]. Wis diajar barang, [x] sêmono ora kapok. He''s been punished and e verything but he still hasn''t learned. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(3883, 'èwèng', 'è wèng : ng-[x] obstinate. ng/di-[x]-[x] or ng- e wang-[x] 1 to push at, keep shoving. 2 to carry around. Saking sênênge dhèke mlaku rana-rene ng-[x]-[x] ijasahe. He''s so happy he carries his diploma e verywhere with him. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(3884, 'èxcèm', 'è xcèm : var sp of È KSIM. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(3885, 'èxposisi', 'è xposisi : e xhibition. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(3886, 'ekor', 'e kor [Ind] : 1 buntut; 2 e nt. perangan kang buri, barisan kang ana ing buri, katêmahaning lêlakon; 3 kanggo wilanganing kewan; meng: 1 kaya buntut; 2 tansah tutburi; diekori: tansah dikinthil. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 5),
(3887, 'ela,elo', 'e la, e lo [Ind] : e lo. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 2),
(3888, 'elak', 'e lak [Ind] : meng: 1 e ndha, ngendhani; 2 ora manut prentah; dielakkan: ditangkis, diendhani. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 4),
(3889, 'elu', 'e lu [Ind] : di- e lukan: dipêthuk, dipapag; kc. alu. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 5),
(3890, 'embik', 'e mbik [Ind] : meng: 1 nywara ê mbèk; 2 mêntul ngêndhêlong tmr. jrambah kayu lsp. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 3),
(3891, 'embun', 'e mbun [Ind] : 1 bun; 2 ing têmbung camboran atêgês lêmbut ut. alus; ber: ngêbun- ê bun (kêkadhar lsp); mengembun: kaya bun, pating jriwut tmr. kuliting wowohan lsp; diembunkan: diêbun- ê bunake. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 8),
(3892, 'embus', 'e mbus [Ind] : 1 abab, angining napas; 2 mlayu nggêblas, minggat; meng: 1 ndamu, ngababi; 2 lunga nggêblas, bubar mlayu tmr. wadyabala lsp; diembuskan: 1 disêbul, didamu; 2 digusah, diurak-urak; e mbusan: 1 ububan; 2 sêmprong. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 5),
(3893, 'empenak', 'e mpenak [Ind] : (pujuk-): têmbung manis (pangrêmih, pangungrum); di: diêla- ê la, ditamani têmbung manis, digumatèni; kc. penak. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 9),
(3894, 'endal', 'e ndal [Ind] : meng: ngênêt- ê nêt (sukêt ing kranjang lsp.). Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 2),
(3895, 'endas', 'e ndas [Ind] : di: dilandhêsake; e ndasan: landhêsan. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 9),
(3896, 'enggan', 'e nggan [Ind] : ê moh, mopo, lênggana, suthik, wêgah. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 9),
(3897, 'engkang', 'e ngkang [Ind] : meng: mlaku e kar. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 10),
(3898, 'entah(kan)', 'e ntah(kan) [Ind] : e mbuh; e ntah- e ntah: saêmbuh (akèh bangêt). Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 3),
(3899, 'entak', 'e ntak [Ind] : meng: 1 ngambruk nggloso; 2 nanggor dhasar tmr. prau; 3 nggêdrug; dientak- e ntakkan: 1 digêdrug-gêdrugake; 2 diêntrog- ê ntrog, digêdhug-gêdhugake tmr. takêran lsp; pengentak: brug (kanggo madhêtake lêmah). Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 7),
(3900, 'enteng', 'e nteng [Ind] : è nthèng. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 10),
(3901, 'esa, sa', 'e sa, sa [Ind] : sawiji; diesakan: disawijèkake; e sa- e saan: e kan, ijèn. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 5),
(3902, 'esot', 'e sot [Ind] : meng: 1 mlaku ngesot; 2 e nt. rindhik bangêt. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 2),
(3903, 'êncakênci', 'ê ncakênci : N.K. ê tre dans une grande joie, ne plus se sentir de joie. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 9),
(3904, 'endah', 'e ndah : Kw. beau, joli, é légant. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 1),
(3905, 'êntyarsa', 'ê ntyarsa : Kw. é nervé, impuissant, débile, insensible. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 6),
(3906, 'ece', 'e ce : N.K. une e spèce de coquillage. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 2),
(3907, 'eroh', 'e roh : e t e ruh , N.K. chancelant, irrésolu, indécis. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3908, 'èrès', 'è rès : N.K. un morceau, une partie d''un tout. ng , couper, trancher, prendre une partie d''un tout. ngèrèsake , N. — kên , couper avec quelque chose, faire couper. e resan , un morceau, fragment. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3909, 'èrèm', 'è rèm : e t orêm , N.K. obscure: incertain; ê tre e mbarrassé. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 4),
(3910, 'edah', 'e dah : Kw. différence, diversité, e t = idah . Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 9),
(3911, 'èdêm', 'è dêm : N.K. é tat de ce qui e st à moitié ouvert. m , ê tre à moitié ouvert (comme une fleur). Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 2),
(3912, 'etuh', 'e tuh : Kw. e au ou liquide qui se trouve dans les fruits. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 10),
(3913, 'êtir', 'ê tir : N.K. poste avancé: pion au jeu d'' é checs. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 4),
(3914, 'ètèr', 'è tèr : N.K. un marchand e n détail. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 10),
(3915, 'êtup', 'ê tup : e t ê tub , N.K. e ntourer de tous côtés, attaquer de tous côtés. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3916, 'êtub', 'ê tub : e t atub , v. ê tup . Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 3),
(3917, 'êsuk', 'ê suk : e t suk , N.K. ng , poursuivre quelqu''un dans toutes les directions. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 4),
(3918, 'estu', 'e stu : K. certitude, vérité. saèstu , certainement, vraiment, véritablement, assurément, e n vérité. ngèstokake , N. — kên , K. assurer, attester; approuver, trouver bon, obéir. pangèstu , approbation, bénédiction. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3919, 'ewuh', 'e wuh : N. è wêd , K. è wêh , Kw. difficile, pénible. pak , N. pakèwêd , K. difficulté, obstacle. ngewuhi , N. ngèwêdi , K. causer des difficultés,
mettre des obstacles à. kewuhan , N. kèwêdan , K. e mbarrassé dans des difficultés. ngewuhake , N. ... selengkapnya e wuh : N. è wêd , K. è wêh , Kw. difficile, pénible. pakewuh , N. pakèwêd , K. difficulté, obstacle. ngewuhi , N. ngèwêdi , K. causer des difficultés, mettre des obstacles à. kewuhan , N. kèwêdan , K. e mbarrassé dans des difficultés. ngewuhake , N. ngèwêdakên , K. causer des difficultés, faire que quelqu''un soit e mbarrassé. makewuh , N. makèwêd , K. e mbarrasser, mettre des obstacles dans un chemin. makewuhi , N. makèwêdi , K. opposer des difficultés à quelqu''un, faire obstacle à. e wuh- e wuhan , N. è wêd- è wêdan , K. e mbarras. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3920, 'êlur', 'ê lur : N.K. une petite e spèce de ver, ver de terre. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 2),
(3921, 'elur', 'e lur : N.K. fourmiller; se diriger e n grand nombre vers une même place. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 1),
(3922, 'êlèk', 'ê lèk : N. l''action de tenir les yeux ouverts, ê tre é veillé. m , tenir les yeux ouverts, veiller, ne pas dormir. ngêlèkake , ouvrir les yeux à quelqu''un, faire que quelqu''un soit veillant. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 3),
(3923, 'elik', 'e lik : N.K. aversion, antipathie, opposition. ngake , N. — kên , K. s''opposer à quelqu''un, e mpêcher. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3924, 'êlung', 'ê lung : N.K. bouton, rejeton. ngêlu , ê tre comme un bouton, comme un rejeton. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 3),
(3925, 'êlèng', 'ê lèng : e t lèng , N.K. un trou dans la terre. anglèng , faire un trou dans la terre. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 6),
(3926, 'êlong', 'ê long : e t long , N.K. diminution, amoindrissement. ng , diminuer, amoindrir. kalong , déduit, diminué, amoindri: diminution. ngêlongi , ôter de quelque chose, diminuer une chose. longana , soit ôté de, soit diminué. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 9),
(3927, 'êpur', 'ê pur : N. se tenir é gal, sans gagner ni perdre. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 9),
(3928, 'êpak', 'ê pak : N.K. ng , acheter beaucoup à la fois, obtenir beaucoup e n même temps. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 3),
(3929, 'êpot', 'ê pot : e t pot , N.K. démission d''un e mploi; changement d''année. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3930, 'êjin', 'ê jin : e t ê jim , un e sprit, un génie, un démon. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 6),
(3931, 'êjim', 'ê jim : v. ê jin . Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 3),
(3932, 'êmar', 'ê mar : e t ê mir , N.K. e ffrayé: timide. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 5),
(3933, 'êmpu', 'ê mpu : N.K. (nom d''une e spèce de tubercule), (particule qui se place devant les noms de personnes comme si , ou pun ). Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 2),
(3934, 'èmpèr', 'è mpèr : N.K. la partie la plus basse: la partie la plus avancée, le frontispice d''une maison. ng , e n bas, vers le bas. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 2),
(3935, 'êmplok', 'ê mplok : N.K. ng , remplir la bouche, contenir dans la bouche. ê mplokan , plein la bouche. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3936, 'êmbek-êmbekan', 'ê mbek- ê mbekan : N.K. e ssayer ses forces contre un autre, ou l''un contre l''autre. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3937, 'èmbèt', 'è mbèt : N.K. ng , appeler q.q. dans une affaire, appeler quelqu''un comme complice. kaèmbèt , e t kèmbèt , cité, appelé, celui qui e st dans une affaire, complice. pangèmbèt , un complice; complicité. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 7),
(3938, 'èmêng', 'è mêng : N.K. chagrin, e nnuie, e mbarras. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 10),
(3939, 'êgar', 'ê gar : N.K. une fleur qui s'' e ntr''ouvre ou qui é clot. m , s'' e ntr''ouvrir, é clore. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 6),
(3940, 'êbur', 'ê bur : N.K. disparaître, se perdre. ng , réduire à rien, faire disparaître. kabur , disparu, e mporté par le vent. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 8),
(3941, 'ebor', 'e bor : N.K. un instrument pour chercher l''or dans la terre ou dans l'' e au. ng , chercher l''or avec cet instrument. pangeboran , une mine d''or. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 9),
(3942, 'ebat', 'e bat : N.K. é tonné: é tonnement, admiration, admirable, surprenant. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 7),
(3943, 'êbang', 'ê bang : N.K. promesse, e ngagement. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 6),
(3944, 'êngak', 'ê ngak : K. ouvrir, desserrer, lâcher. ang , ouvrir quelque chose, (p. e x. une porte). angêngakakên , faire ouvrir. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 9),
(3945, 'dènèstrèni', 'dèn è strèni : Kw. ê tre approuvé, v. è stri . Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 5),
(3946, 'ngèlèg-èlègi', 'ngèlèg- è lègi : N.K. e njôler, allêcher. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 9),
(3947, 'ngêmbak-êmbak', 'ngêmbak- ê mbak : N.K. réduire e n petits morceaux. Dictionnaire Javanais-Français, L''Abbé P. Favre, 1870, #917.', 7),
(3948, 'eih', 'e ih () : hihih. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 5),
(3949, 'èhèh', 'è hèh (EhEh) : hehe, hahhah, hèhhèh, Ahahah, hahahah, hayay, OmOm, homhom, Umom, humom, dikhah, dhikhah, mom. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 10),
(3950, 'Èhèhèh', 'È hèhèh (EhEhEh) : cehaha. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 5),
(3951, 'ehehe', 'e hehe () : UhUh, Ahodha, hehahcehah, cehacehah. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 1),
(3952, 'èêm', 'è êm (E|m) : II. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 10),
(3953, 'encok', 'e ncok (encO?) : [m]: coda, mapihêr. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 10),
(3954, 'endrasuta', 'e ndrasuta (endrOsutO) : jêjuluke panêngahing pandhawa. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 1),
(3955, 'êndhok', 'ê ndhok (|nDO?) : triha, indhik; [mindhik-mindhik]: manyakman. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 1),
(3956, 'êrut', 'ê rut (|rUt) : [ng]: miyungyung. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 2),
(3957, 'erang', 'e rang (eraG) : [m]: umiras. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 2),
(3958, 'êdêd', 'ê dêd (|d|d) : [m]: mêsês, musus, myus. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 2),
(3959, 'êdus', 'ê dus (|dUs) : basu. Bausastra: Jarwa Kawi, Padmasusastra, 1903, #11.', 1),
