(6807, 'instrumêntalia', 'i nstrumêntalia : i nstrumental (gamelan) music. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(6808, 'intar', 'i ntar : oj metaphor( i c). See also ENTAR. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(6809, 'intènsip', 'i ntènsip : i ntensive. ng/di-[x]-(ake) to i ntensify. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(6810, 'intêrnir', 'i ntêrnir : 1 person who i s i nterned. 2 place where e.g. enemy aliens are i nterned. ng/di-[x] to i ntern. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(6811, 'intêrpiu', 'i ntêrpiu : i nterview. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(6812, 'inthik', 'i nthik : i nthak-[x] to keep coming and going, to move back and forth constantly. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(6813, 'intip', 'i ntip : scorched rice at the bottom of the pan. m-[x]-m-[x] to be i n sight just at the top. Sirahe ketok m-[x]-m-[x]. Only the top of his head showed. ng-[x] 1 forming a scorched layer of rice at the bottom of the pan. 2 (psv di-[x]) to peek (at). [x]- i ng nraka the wickedest souls of all. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(6814, 'intir', 'i ntir : m-[x](-m-[x]) low, flickering; on and off. Digangsa mawa gêni kang m-[x]-m-[x] wae. Fry i t over a very low fire. lara pilêk sing lumintu m-[x] (to have) colds one right after the other. ng-[x]-[x] 1 i ntsfr hungry. luwe ng-[x]-[x] famished. 2 (psv di-[x]-[x]) to hand sth out little by little. ... selengkapnya i ntir : m-[x](-m-[x]) low, flickering; on and off. Digangsa mawa gêni kang m-[x]-m-[x] wae. Fry i t over a very low fire. lara pilêk sing lumintu m-[x] (to have) colds one right after the other. ng-[x]-[x] 1 i ntsfr hungry. luwe ng-[x]-[x] famished. 2 (psv di-[x]-[x]) to hand sth out little by little. ng/di-[x](-[x])-ake 1 to lower [a cooking fire]. 2 to give [things] out i n small amounts. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(6815, 'incak', 'i ncak : var of I DAK. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(6816, 'inci', 'i nci : i nch. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(6817, 'incim', 'i ncim : [x]-[x]-an to threaten each other. ng/di-[x]-[x] to threaten, i ntimidate. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(6818, 'incip', 'i ncip : var of I CIP. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(6819, 'incrit', 'i ncrit : ng/di-[x]-[x] to give out i n small amounts. Nyauri utang bae di-[x]-[x]. He repaid the loan little by little. A ng-[x]-[x] olèhe nganggo banyune supaya awèt. A uses the water sparingly so as to conserve i t. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(6820, 'ipah', 'i pah : 1 grated coconut mixed i nto coconut sap during coconut-sugar processing. 2 earnings (sbst kr for OPAH). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
