(11371, 'oyog', 'o yog : ng/di-[x](-[x]) to shake sth. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(11372, 'oyok', 'o yok : [x]-[x]-an to chase after, hunt down. Saiki para mudha [x]-[x]-an pêgawean. Young people are going after jobs these days. ng/di-[x](-[x]) to cluster around sth. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(11373, 'okèr', 'o kèr : ng/di-[x](-[x]) to scratch [sand, soil]. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(11374, 'ollah', 'o llah : see DAT. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(11375, 'omèl', 'o mèl : ng-[x] to grumble at, nag. ng/di-[x]-ake 1 to grumble about sth. 2 cr to talk about sth. ng/di-[x]-i to grouse at, complain to. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(11376, 'ondhêrdhil', 'o ndhêrdhil : mechanical part. [x] pit bicycle parts. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(11377, 'ondhol', 'o ndhol : sloppy, coarse, gross. ng-[x] cr to chase girls. ng/di-[x]-i to examine [poultry] to determine whether it can reproduce. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(11378, 'onggo', 'o nggo : ng-[x]-[x] to weep long and bitterly. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(11379, 'onggrok', 'o nggrok : ng/di-[x]-[x]-ake to leave sth unattended to. Dhèke ng-[x]-[x]-ake pêgaweyane wis ana sêminggu. He''s neglected his work for a week now. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
