(11381, 'ongol', 'o ngol : [x]-[x] a gelatine-like food eaten with shredded coconut. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(11382, 'oncèk', 'o ncèk : [x]-an peeled, pared. urang [x]-an shelled shrimp. ng/di-[x]-(i) 1 to peel, pare. 2 to reveal, disclose. ng-[x]-i wadi to give away a secret. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(11383, 'oncit', 'o ncit : ng/di-[x]-[x] to chase. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(11384, 'opak', 'o pak : ng-[x] to make a certain wafer-like snack food. [x] angin the above snack. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(11385, 'oplèt', 'o plèt : antiquated car used as a city taxi with a given route. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(11386, 'orang-utan', 'o rang-utan : large anthropoid ape. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(11387, 'orog', 'o rog : ng/di-[x]-[x] to shake sth. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(11388, 'orok', 'o rok : [x]-[x] a plant that produces a pea-like vegetable. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(11389, 'orot', 'o rot : ng/di-[x]-[x] to use wastefully. ng-[x]-[x] banyu to waste water. Ngirit-irit malah dadi ng-[x]-[x]. I try to save money but it slips right through my fingers. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
