(11967, 'kyanapatih', 'kyana p atih (kyOnO patIh) : p atih. Kawi - Jarwa, Poerwadarminta, 1943, #1856.', 3),
(11968, 'pantun wulu', 'p antun wulu (pantUn wulu) : mênthik | kontulan | mênuran | garêman | sampang | jrabangan | mênthik wangèn | uwèn | p apaharèn | brêngos | nêtêp | p êndhok wêsi | sêngkawa | lêmbayungan | răndha mèntèr | dhudha ngasag | sokanandi | genjah ragi | gewal | jambean | găndapura | drèngès | umbuk | jaka bolot | p rawan antih | urab-urab ... selengkapnya p antun wulu (pantUn wulu) : mênthik | kontulan | mênuran | garêman | sampang | jrabangan | mênthik wangèn | uwèn | p apaharèn | brêngos | nêtêp | p êndhok wêsi | sêngkawa | lêmbayungan | răndha mèntèr | dhudha ngasag | sokanandi | genjah ragi | gewal | jambean | găndapura | drèngès | umbuk | jaka bolot | p rawan antih | urab-urab | manjangan manglar | monteyan | bulêt | bale rante | salamêt | balean. [nama jinising p antun wulu]. Kawi Dasanama, Anonim, 1882, #1905.', 5),
(11969, 'pantun cêmpa', 'p antun cêmpa (pantUn c|mpO) : cêmpa kirana | cêmpa monthèl | cêmpa utri | cêmpa lombok | cêmpa mriyi | cêmpa gêlo | cêmpa kunir | cêmpa lêmbayungan | cêmpa ganggasan | cêmpa mênur | cêmpa wangèn | cêmpa arès | cêmpa klèwèr | cêmpa slamêt | cêmpa kapasan | cêmpa keyong | cêmpa wadêr | cêmpa dêlêg | cêmpa mèlèr | cêmpa dringo | ... selengkapnya p antun cêmpa (pantUn c|mpO) : cêmpa kirana | cêmpa monthèl | cêmpa utri | cêmpa lombok | cêmpa mriyi | cêmpa gêlo | cêmpa kunir | cêmpa lêmbayungan | cêmpa ganggasan | cêmpa mênur | cêmpa wangèn | cêmpa arès | cêmpa klèwèr | cêmpa slamêt | cêmpa kapasan | cêmpa keyong | cêmpa wadêr | cêmpa dêlêg | cêmpa mèlèr | cêmpa dringo | cêmpa kopèk. [nama jinising p antun cêmpa]. Kawi Dasanama, Anonim, 1882, #1905.', 9),
(11970, 'pantun kêtan', 'p antun kêtan (pantUn k|tan) : kêtan sênggaringan, kêtan gajih | kêtan serang | kêtan lumbu | kêtan p uwan | kêtan kuwuk | kêcêlêng | kêtan gondhil | kêtan p ondhoh | kêtan genjah | kêtan p onggok | kêtan urang | kêtan kêpok | kêtan singkal | kêtan sobrah. [nama jinising p antun kêtan]. Kawi Dasanama, Anonim, 1882, #1905.', 2),
(11971, 'pal', 'p al : 1 measure of distance: ca. 0.93 mile = 1507 meters. 2 marker p laced at one- p al intervals along a road. ngê/di-[x] convinced that sth undesirable will take p lace. B ngê yèn aku ora isa lulus ujian. B was sure I couldn''t p ass the exam. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(11972, 'panji', 'p anji : 1 a group of stories, depicted in wayang gêdhog tales, about the Javanese p rince P anji. 2 oj flag. [x] klanthung an unemployed p erson. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(11973, 'Panca Sila', 'P anca Sila : the Five P rinciples on which the Indonesian Republic is based. See also P ANCA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(11974, 'paripurna', 'p aripurna : 1 finished, over. 2 ( p rn p aripurna) complete, p lenary. p asamuan [x] or sidang [x] p lenary session. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(11975, 'pasa', 'p asa : ng, siyam kr 1 to fast. Olèhe [x] kuwat limalas dina. He fasted rigidly for fifteen days. Aku dikon [x] nalika wêtêngku lara. He told me not to eat anything when I had a stomach ache. 2 ng kr ninth month of the Moslem calendar: the fasting month. m/di-[x]-ni to fast for [a certain objective]. ... selengkapnya p asa : ng, siyam kr 1 to fast. Olèhe [x] kuwat limalas dina. He fasted rigidly for fifteen days. Aku dikon [x] nalika wêtêngku lara. He told me not to eat anything when I had a stomach ache. 2 ng kr ninth month of the Moslem calendar: the fasting month. m/di-[x]-ni to fast for [a certain objective]. Dhèwèke masani kanggo anake karêbèn bisa lulus ujiane. She fasted [as a form of p rayer] so that her son would p ass his examinations. [x] ng-asar to fast until 4 P .M. [x] m-bêdhug to fast until 12 noon. [x] n-dina to fast until 6 P .M. [x] manuk to have breakfast early rather than fasting (during P asa month). [x] tutup kêndhang to fast on only the first and last days of the fasting month. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(11976, 'pastèl', 'p astèl : 1 p astel, drawing chalk. 2 a meat-filled p astry. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(11977, 'pati-rasa', 'p ati-rasa : anesthesia. m/di-[x] to anesthetize. mati-rasa gusi to deaden the gum. See also P ATI a . Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(11978, 'pènèt', 'p ènèt : p ênèt, m/di-[x] to squash, flatten. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(11979, 'pêncak', 'p êncak : Javanese-style karate: self-defense system and stylized art form. m-[x] to engage in p êncak. m-[x]-m-[x] inf furious, enraged. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(11980, 'pêncèngèl', 'p êncèngèl : p êncêngèl, p tg [x] p l standing out p rominently. m-[x] sg as above. See also CÈNGÈL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(11981, 'pêrbal', 'p êrbal : a summons, subpoena. m/di-[x] to investigate officially; to make a report on. See also P ROSÈS- P ÊRBAL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(11982, 'pêrwira', 'p êrwira : 1 mighty, p owerful, courageous. 2 ( p rn p êrwira) military officer from lieutenant up. ka-[x]-n courage; might. adu ka-[x]-n p itting their bravery against each other. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(11983, 'planèl', 'p lanèl : p lanêl, flannel. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(11984, 'pramugara', 'p ramugara : p ramugara, male steward. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(11985, 'pramuka', 'p ramuka : p ramuka, Boy or Girl Scout. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(11986, 'profèsor', 'p rofèsor : p rofesor, p rofessor (academic rank). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(11987, 'purba', 'p urba : ancient. [x] kala ancient times. kang m-[x] God. See also P URBA-WISESA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(11988, 'purba-wasesa', 'p urba-wasesa : var of P URBA-WISESA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(11989, 'rudha-paripêksa', 'rudha- p aripêksa : oj ng/di-[x] to force, compel. See also P ARIPÊKSA, RODA. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(11990, 'um-pim-pah', 'um- p im- p ah : an informal method by which more than two p eople settle something: p layed like UM- P ING-SUT (below), except that with the count of p ah all bring down a flat hand, either p alm down or p alm up: matching p alms, the odd man is out, and the p rocess is repeated until all but two have been eliminated. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(11991, 'pacul', 'p acul [Ind] : I di: diplothot, dipèjèt supaya mêcothot. II p acul. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 2),
(11992, 'padam', 'p adam [Ind] : I sirêp, mati tmr. gêni; dikan: dipatèni tmr. gêni, disirêp. II kêmbang trate; merah p adam: abang bangêt. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 7),
(11993, 'padang', 'p adang [Ind] : ara-ara; p adang tiah: sagara wêdhi, ara-ara samun. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 5),
(11994, 'padau', 'p adau [Ind] : layar p adau: layar kanggone yèn nuju p rahara. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 9),
(11995, 'padi', 'p adi [Ind] : I p ari. II cilik tmr. wowohan, up. nyiur p adi. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 10),
(11996, 'paduka', 'p aduka [Ind] : p aduka (kanggo sêbutan). Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 10),
(11997, 'paedah', 'p aedah [Ind] : p aedah, p iguna; ber: maedahi, migunani. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 8),
(11998, 'pagar', 'p agar [Ind] : p agêr, bêthèk; p agar bulan: kalangan (rêmbulan). Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 5),
(11999, 'pair', 'p air [Ind] : p erahu p air: p rau kang dianggo rondha. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 1),
