(14722, 'tăndha mantri', 't ăndha mantri (tOnDO mantri) : mantri t ăndha. Inggih punika ingkang kapitadosan dados juru pamupu beyaning pêkên. Kawi Dasanama, Anonim, 1882, #1905.', 7),
(14723, '-tab', 't a b : (-nta after vowel) ltry your. anak- t a your child. putra-nta your child. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(14724, 'thak', 't hak : rpr a hard object striking a firm surface. Watune diuncalake ing bolongan mau, muni: [x]! He t hrew t he stone into t he hole and it went t hak! [x]-[x]-an t o move restlessly about disturbing others. See also T HIK a , T HUK. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(14725, 'tank', 't ank : (prn t èng) t ank. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(14726, 'tape', 't ape : a sweet food made from fermented sticky rice or cassava. [x] kaspa t his food made with cassava. n/di-[x] t o make [ingredients] into t ape. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(14727, 'tapir', 't apir : t apir (animal). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(14728, 'tau-rasa', 't au-rasa : excl of satisfaction at smn''s similar discomfiture. T au-rasa, saiki kowe ngêrti dhewe piye rasane wong disiksa. Now you see what it feels like t o be t ortured! Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(14729, 'têbu', 't êbu : sugar cane (ros-an kr). [x] t êlung lonjor t hree stalks of sugar cane. t êbu sa(ê)ros one piece (between joints) of sugar cane. gilingan [x] sugar mill. banyune [x] sugar-cane liquid (for processing into sugar). [x]-n land planted t o sugar cane. n-[x] (ng-ros-an kr) t o plant sugar cane. pa-[x]-n ... selengkapnya t êbu : sugar cane (ros-an kr). [x] t êlung lonjor t hree stalks of sugar cane. t êbu sa(ê)ros one piece (between joints) of sugar cane. gilingan [x] sugar mill. banyune [x] sugar-cane liquid (for processing into sugar). [x]-n land planted t o sugar cane. n-[x] (ng-ros-an kr) t o plant sugar cane. pa-[x]-n (pa-ros-an kr) land planted t o sugar cane. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(14730, 'tèlkim', 't èlkim : rg var of T ÊLKIM. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(14731, 'tên', 't ên : inf var of BOTÊN, WONTÊN. T ên won. T here aren'' t any. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(14732, 'thêngèl', 't hêngèl : var of T HÈNGÈL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(14733, 'tenggok', 't enggok : t ènggok, small deep basket of woven bamboo. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(14734, 'tenong', 't enong : t ènong, a round covered box of woven bamboo, used esp. for keeping pastries. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(14735, 'tèrmos', 't èrmos : t êrmos, t hermos bottle. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(14736, 'tètèg', 't ètèg : bar, barrier (var of T ÊTÊG). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(14737, 'thêthêl', 't hêthêl : var of T HÈTHÈL. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(14738, 'thingb', 't hing b : (or [x]-[x]) utterly, completely, t hrough and t rough. Wis êntèk [x]. It''s all gone! jaka [x]-[x] a confirmed bachelor. See also T HOKTHING, T HONG- T HING. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 1),
(14739, 'tonb', 't on b : 1 metric t on (1,000 kilograms = ca. 2200 lbs). 2 unit of area (1 square meter = ca. 0.84 square yard. 3 monetary unit (1,000 rupiahs). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(14740, 'tut-wuri', 't ut-wuri : var of T UT-BURI. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(14741, 'bukutangan', 'buku t angan [Ind] : ugêl-ugêl t angan. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 8),
(14742, 'bulanterang', 'bulan t erang [Ind] : ( t êrang bulan) padhang rêmbulan. Bausastra Indonesia-Jawi, Purwadarminta, c. 1939, #1979.', 1),
