(16466, 'pandhitawadon', 'pandhita w adon (panDitO wadOn) : brahmani, padhane: arimba: arimbi | apsara: apsari | narèswara: narèswari | rasêksa: rasêksi | ditya: dityi | w idadara: w idadari | w i (pi) sawa (sawi) | bramana: bramani mau. Campur Bawur, Padmasusastra, 1935, #248.', 9),
(16467, 'walikat', 'w alikat () : KN. | Antaraning têpak kiwa têngên sadhuwuring w atês kêmbên mungguhing w ong w adon. voorb. | Kang ana w ulu w alikat, w ulu lêmbut pratăndha tuhwèng janji, lawan lêpas budinipun, ... zie TS. Iman Sapingi pangkur pungkasan. | Sinuduk jajanya trus w alikat kering. Kawruh Kamanungsan, Wirapustaka, c. 1900, #252.', 5),
(16468, 'wadung', 'w adung (wadUG) : axe; madung: to cut w ith an axe. Giri Sonta Course for Javanese (Lexicon), Bakker, 1964, #286.', 6),
(16469, 'witikna', 'w itikna (witI?nO) : Ng., w itikna Kr.; w hat w ill you say. Giri Sonta Course for Javanese (Lexicon), Bakker, 1964, #286.', 8),
(16470, 'wêkasane', 'w êkasane (w|kasane) : Ng., w êkasanipun Kr.; finally. Giri Sonta Course for Javanese (Lexicon), Bakker, 1964, #286.', 6),
(16471, 'ndhrodhogwèl-wèlan', 'ndhrodhog w èl- w èlan (nDrODOg wEl­wElan) : Ng.; to tremble w ith fear. Giri Sonta Course for Javanese (Lexicon), Bakker, 1964, #286.', 6),
(16472, 'dinawêton', 'dina w êton (dinO w|tOn) : Ng., w êdalan, w iyosan, tingalan Kr.; birthday. Giri Sonta Course for Javanese (Lexicon), Bakker, 1964, #286.', 7),
(16473, 'wong saomah', 'w ong saomah (wOG saomah) : sabrayat, sabatin; the w hole family. Giri Sonta Course for Javanese (Lexicon), Bakker, 1964, #286.', 9),
