(16591, 'yatim', 'y atim : fatherless; orphaned. omah [x] orphanage. bocah/anak [x] fatherless child; child whose father died before he was born; orphan. [x] piatu orphan, i.e. child with neither parent living. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(16592, 'yatra', 'y atra : money (sbst? kr for DHUWIT). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(16593, 'yauk', 'y a''uk : ora [x] slang no good; unattractive. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
