(16598, 'yêm', 'y êm : ngê/di-[x] to keep moist, prevent from drying out. ngê/di-[x]-[x]-(i) to free oneself of troubles. Atine di-[x]-[x]. He calmed himself down. See also AYÊM. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(16599, 'yêr', 'y êr : [x]-[x]-an dizzy; nauseated. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(16600, 'yèt', 'y èt : (prn jèt) jet. motor mabur [x] jet plane. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(16601, 'yiyid', 'y iyid : sticky substance. Êndhog kodhok digandhèng nganggo [x]. Frogs'' eggs are held in masses by sticky stuff. ng-[x] in a sticky condition. Jangane wis ng-[x]. The vegetables are oozing decayed matter. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(16602, 'yiyis', 'y iyis : ng-[x] [of rain] incessant. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(16603, 'yo', 'y o : ng come on! let''s ... ! (shf of AYO). [x], ndang dhahar [x]! Come on - let''s hurry up and eat! Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 4),
(16604, 'yodhêmporêm', 'y odhêmporêm : iodoform. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 8),
(16605, 'yodium', 'y odium : iodine. [x] tingtur tincture of iodine. ng/di-[x] to treat with iodine. Tatune wis di-[x]. He put iodine on his cut. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 3),
(16606, 'yojana', 'y ojana : measure of distance: ca. 1507 metters = ca. 93 mile. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(16607, 'Yogyakarta', 'Y ogyakarta : central Javanese city, former kingdom and still the site of the court headed by the Sultan, and one of the two major cultural centers (see also SURAKARTA). nga-[x] Hayuningrat the complete formal name of this city. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(16608, 'yok', 'y ok : [x] (n)apa rg how? how come? Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(16609, 'yom', 'y om : [x]-[x]-an that which is shaded or sheltered. turu awan ing [x]-[x]-an to take a nap in the shade. kê-[x]-ên overshaded; overprotected. ngê-[x] 1 to cast shade; to create shelter. 2 to take shelter from sun, rain. ngê/di-[x]-i to shade/shelter/protect sth. pa-[x]-an protection, shelter. pa-[x]-an ... selengkapnya y om : [x]-[x]-an that which is shaded or sheltered. turu awan ing [x]-[x]-an to take a nap in the shade. kê-[x]-ên overshaded; overprotected. ngê-[x] 1 to cast shade; to create shelter. 2 to take shelter from sun, rain. ngê/di-[x]-i to shade/shelter/protect sth. pa-[x]-an protection, shelter. pa-[x]-an kewan an animal shelter. pa-ngê-[x]-an 1 a shaded place. 2 protector, patron. 3 act or way of protecting/sheltering. See also AYOM. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(16610, 'yuda', 'y uda : ltry war, battle. pa-[x]-n oj battlefield. [x] nêgara 1 administration of the country. 2 etiquette. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(16611, 'yuman', 'y uman : ka-[x]-an oj happiness, well-being. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(16612, 'Yunani', 'Y unani : pertaining to Greece. nêgara [x] Greece. têmbung sing asale saka têmbung [x] words of Greek origin. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
(16613, 'yungta', 'y ungta : aunt (parent''s older sister) (shc from BIYUNG ANTA). Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 6),
(16614, 'yur', 'y ur : [x]-[x]-an to sway flexibly. Wit-witan [x]-[x]-an kêtrajang angin gêdhe. The trees swayed in the high wind. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 5),
(16615, 'yuri', 'y uri : 1 jury. 2 umpire, referee. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(16616, 'yuris', 'y uris : lawyer. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 2),
(16617, 'yustisi', 'y ustisi : justice. pangadilan [x] a court of justice. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 9),
(16618, 'yuta', 'y uta : million. [x]-n (numbering in the) millions. Dhuwite [x]-n cacahe. He''s worth millions. pra-[x] -millionth. sa pra-[x]. 000001. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 10),
(16619, 'yutun', 'y utun : hardworking, dedicated. tani [x] a true dedicated farmer. Javanese-English Dictionary, Horne, 1974, #1968.', 7),
